---
import ServicePage from '../components/ServicePage.astro';
---

<ServicePage
  slug="fractional-revops"
  title="Fractional RevOps: Senior Revenue Operations Without the Full-Time Cost"
  description="Embedded fractional RevOps for $2-10M businesses. A dedicated ops roadmap, CRM ownership, and cross-functional coordination at 20-30% the cost of a full-time hire."
  serviceName="Fractional RevOps"
  serviceTag="Fractional RevOps"
  serviceSchemaDescription="Embedded fractional revenue operations leadership. Dedicated ops roadmap, CRM management, reporting health, and cross-functional coordination at a fraction of the cost of a full-time VP."
  headlineParts={['Senior revenue ops ownership,', 'without the VP price tag.']}
  subtitle="Your part-time VP of RevOps, without the full-time cost or the six-month hiring process."
  hook="Growing companies between $2M and $10M ARR consistently hit the same wall: ops work piling up on the founder or head of sales, a CRM nobody trusts, and no one with the seniority to own the revenue system end-to-end. A full-time VP of RevOps costs $150-200K+ base and takes months to hire. A Salesforce admin executes tasks but doesn't own strategy. Fractional fills the gap: senior ownership and actual execution, at a fraction of the cost."
  whatsIncluded={[
    'Dedicated ops roadmap aligned to your revenue goals and quarterly priorities',
    'Weekly standup attendance and async availability throughout the month',
    'Cross-functional coordination between sales, marketing, and finance operations',
    'Ongoing CRM management, reporting health, and process iteration',
  ]}
  goodFitIf={[
    "You're scaling past $2M ARR and ops is becoming a bottleneck, not a tailwind",
    'Your founder or head of sales is spending too much time on ops work themselves',
    'You want senior ownership of the revenue stack, not task execution',
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "What's the difference between fractional RevOps and a full-time hire?",
      htmlA: "A full-time VP of RevOps costs $150-200K+ base, takes 3-6 months to hire, and is typically overkill until you're well past $10M ARR. Fractional gives you the same senior thinking and execution at 20-30% of the cost, with a clear exit when you're ready to bring it in-house.",
    },
    {
      q: 'How much time does fractional RevOps actually require from me?',
      htmlA: 'Minimal. The point is to take work off your plate, not add to it. Expect a 30-minute weekly sync and occasional async questions. Everything else is handled.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What does a typical engagement look like month to month?',
      htmlA: 'Month one is a structured discovery and roadmap. From there: weekly standups, async execution on the ops backlog, regular reporting health checks, and a monthly review of priorities. Everything is documented so nothing is a black box.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How much does fractional RevOps cost?',
      htmlA: 'Fractional RevOps runs as a monthly or quarterly retainer with a 3-month minimum, sized to the level of ongoing ownership you need. See the <a href="/pricing" class="link-teal">engagement models</a>, then book a call so we can share a precise number against your situation.',
    },
  ]}
  relatedServices={[
    { slug: 'crm-implementation', title: 'CRM Implementation & Cleanup', sub: 'Salesforce or HubSpot built right' },
    { slug: 'reporting-analytics', title: 'Reporting & Analytics', sub: 'Dashboards that drive decisions' },
    { slug: 'process-automation', title: 'Workflows & Automation', sub: 'Replace manual work with systems' },
  ]}
  ctaHeadline="Ready to talk specifics?"
  ctaBody="Book a free 30-minute call. No pitch, no proposal. An honest conversation about whether this is the right fit for your situation."
  heroImage="/images/hero-fractional-revops.jpg"
/>
